802101f serialhdl: accept socket:// serial ports (TCP UART bridge)
020d25e probe: Disable axis twist compensation for nozzle probes
From 802101f2d4d5e3e36e8597adc49fee7fe9965ceb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mcsketch <calebkuhlman94@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:57:39 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] serialhdl: accept socket:// serial ports (TCP UART bridge)

The AD4 SoC exposes the MCU UART through ad4-bridge on TCP :5000. Let
[mcu] serial: socket://host:port open through pyserial serial_for_url;
skip RTS and the stk500v2 leave sequence, which need a real tty.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 klippy/serialhdl.py | 22 ++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/klippy/serialhdl.py b/klippy/serialhdl.py
index adc5916..4be6e32 100644
--- a/klippy/serialhdl.py
+++ b/klippy/serialhdl.py
@@ -190,18 +190,28 @@ class SerialReader:
         while 1:
             if self.reactor.monotonic() > start_time + 90.:
                 self._error("Unable to connect")
+            is_socket = serialport.startswith("socket://")
             try:
-                serial_dev = serial.Serial(baudrate=baud, timeout=0,
-                                           exclusive=True)
-                serial_dev.port = serialport
-                serial_dev.rts = rts
-                serial_dev.open()
+                if is_socket:
+                    # TCP bridge to a remote UART (e.g. AD4 SoC ad4-bridge):
+                    # pyserial's socket:// handler; fd is a plain socket, so
+                    # no RTS/termios handling applies.
+                    serial_dev = serial.serial_for_url(serialport,
+                                                       baudrate=baud,
+                                                       timeout=0)
+                else:
+                    serial_dev = serial.Serial(baudrate=baud, timeout=0,
+                                               exclusive=True)
+                    serial_dev.port = serialport
+                    serial_dev.rts = rts
+                    serial_dev.open()
             except (OSError, IOError, serial.SerialException) as e:
                 logging.warning("%sUnable to open serial port: %s",
                              self.warn_prefix, e)
                 self.reactor.pause(self.reactor.monotonic() + 5.)
                 continue
-            stk500v2_leave(serial_dev, self.reactor)
+            if not is_socket:
+                stk500v2_leave(serial_dev, self.reactor)
             ret = self._start_session(serial_dev)
             if ret:
                 break
